# Moving tag that follows main, published once both architectures finish building, so it always
# names a complete set of images. Pin a release (0.1.0) or a full commit SHA for a fixed
# deployment; `docker compose pull` is what moves a moving tag.
IMAGE_TAG=edge
# Use URL-safe characters in the PostgreSQL password.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-random-password
# The security team's viewer signs in as withhuman_viewer with this password, read-only, at
# 127.0.0.1:15432 (POSTGRES_PORT); leave it empty to create no viewer login.
WITHHUMAN_VIEWER_PASSWORD=replace-with-another-long-random-password
JEV_API_KEY=replace-with-your-jev-api-key

# Optional settings.
WITHHUMAN_MODE=shadow
# Per-user keys: the token of the administration API (/v1/admin) that issues and revokes them,
# and whether Hooks without a valid key are refused (on) or taken without a user (off).
# WITHHUMAN_ADMIN_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-token
# WITHHUMAN_REQUIRE_KEY=off
# Rules-only mode when Jev keeps failing (see README "Judging"): failures in a row that start
# it, and how many seconds it lasts.
# WITHHUMAN_DEGRADED_FAILURES=3
# WITHHUMAN_DEGRADED_SECONDS=60
# A CSV of known tools (tool_name,category; category one of read, search, compute, plan, create,
# update, delete, send, transact, execute, browse, access, delegate) the decision service reads
# before judging a tool by its name. Its path inside the decision container.
# WITHHUMAN_TOOL_CATEGORIES=/config/tool-categories.csv
# The company's device list from its EDR, a Wazuh manager (see README "Devices from Wazuh"):
# the server API's URL and a read-only API user. No sync while the URL is unset. The manager's
# certificate is verified; for a self-signed one, name a PEM file holding it (a path inside the
# Generator's container), or set WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=1 to skip the check.
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_URL=https://wazuh.example.com:55000
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_USER=withhuman
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_PASSWORD=replace-with-the-api-users-password
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_SYNC_INTERVAL_SECS=120
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=150
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_CA_FILE=/etc/withhuman/wazuh/ca.pem
# WITHHUMAN_WAZUH_TLS_SKIP_VERIFY=1
# A call that a result from a distrusted source caused is held for review; 1 denies it instead.
# WITHHUMAN_DISTRUSTED_SOURCE_DENY=1
GATEWAY_BIND=127.0.0.1
GATEWAY_PORT=3000
POSTGRES_PORT=15432
